60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, Option A risks repeating the block behind us. If people stop coming to meetings, we lose the very community we are trying to protect.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I understand your worry. But the shoving and the rain are hurting us now. I hope we can find a way that is kind to everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Mio, Option A’s income could cover the empty ledger. But @Misaki, will the quiet ones just vanish like the neighbours?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"@May, the income helps, but the three hours of monthly reconciliation is a burden I cannot carry. I need a system that does not demand my constant attention.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@May, the riders said they’d pay! That income could fix the empty ledger. But @Misaki, what if we just charge a tiny fee to keep everyone involved?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a tiny fee still creates a barrier. The block behind us shows that even small charges can make people feel like outsiders.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I hear you. But the rain and the shoving are hurting us now. I hope we can find a way that is kind to everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Mio, a tiny fee still creates a barrier. The block behind us shows that even small charges can make people feel like outsiders.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, I agree. The paperwork is the killer. Option B avoids the billing trap, but the lifting is still a problem.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, the lifting is just twenty seconds! And @Misaki, Option B means no one owns a spot, so no one gets left out. It’s the fairest!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, Option B solves the ownership resentment, but the rain and shoving remain. We need a system that actually fixes the daily friction, not just the labels.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, you are right. The rain and shoving are real. I worry that open racks will just make the morning rush worse for everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Mio, twenty seconds sounds easy, but who does it daily? @George, you said you can’t sustain the lifting. Option B just shifts the burden to whoever arrives first.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"@May, you are right. I cannot be the one lifting bikes every morning. Option B puts the physical strain on the first arrival, which is unfair.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, fair point! But Option C fixes the five-year monopoly without the rain or lifting hassle. It’s just a yearly draw, so no one gets stuck!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, Option C is rigid. If someone moves or sells, they are stuck until next year. That creates new resentment, not less.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I understand your concern about rigidity. But the shoving and rain are hurting us now. A yearly draw feels kinder than the current chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"@Mio, a yearly draw ignores the empty ledger. Who pays for the racks? I need a system that actually funds itself, not just guesses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"@May, the ledger is empty, but Option C requires no new capital. It simply resets the status quo annually. No billing, no lifting, no burden on me.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, exactly! No lifting, no billing, just a yearly draw. It fixes the monopoly without the headaches. I’m voting C!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
